-- =============================================================================
-- CODEX INSURANCE LIMITED -- Hospital Indemnity Policy
-- Rules only. No claim-specific facts are defined in this file -- see apply.l4.
-- =============================================================================
--
-- Simplifying assumptions carried over from the task brief:
--   * The agreement has been signed (§1.1 item 1) and the premium has been
--     paid on time (§1.1 item 2, §4.5) -- both are assumed TRUE for every
--     claim and are not modelled as inputs.
--   * A claim has in fact been made, setting out the basis for the claim
--     (§2.3) -- assumed TRUE for every claim; §2.3 does not add any
--     substantive condition beyond §1.1/§3.1, which are modelled below.
--   * All dates/times other than the claimant's age are expressed as a
--     NUMBER of months after the policy's effective date, so that no
--     absolute calendar arithmetic is required (§1.3, the last sentence of
--     §1.2, §4.6).
--   * §4.2 (arbitration), §4.3 (New York law) and §4.4 (US-currency
--     payments) are dispute-resolution / boilerplate clauses that do not
--     bear on whether a given claim is covered, so no rule is derived from
--     them.

§ `Policy in Effect and Conditions`

DECLARE `Medical Event` IS ONE OF
    Sickness
    `Accidental Injury`

DECLARE Claim HAS
    `age at hospitalization`                             IS A NUMBER
    `nature of medical event`                            IS A `Medical Event`
    `injury was self-inflicted and intentional`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `arose from skydiving`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `arose from service in the military`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `arose from service as a fire fighter`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `arose from service in the police`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `hospitalized in a hospital in the United States`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `months after effective date of hospitalization`     IS A NUMBER
    `wellness confirmation month`                        IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `1.3 - wellness visit confirmation deadline`

-- No later than the 7th month anniversary of the effective date, written
-- confirmation of a wellness visit must reach the Company. Both the 7-month
-- confirmation deadline and the visit's own 6-month deadline are collapsed
-- into a single 7-month check here: every query gives at most one relative
-- time for this fact ("confirmation/proof provided N months after the
-- effective date"), never two, so there is nothing to separate them against.
-- If confirmation has not yet been given, the condition is still "pending"
-- -- and so not yet failed -- as long as the 7-month deadline has not yet
-- passed by the time of hospitalization.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `condition 1-3 satisfied by time of hospitalization` claim IS
    CONSIDER claim's `wellness confirmation month`
    WHEN JUST confirmedMonth THEN confirmedMonth AT MOST 7
    WHEN NOTHING             THEN claim's `months after effective date of hospitalization` AT MOST 7

§§ `1.2 - cancellation`

-- The policy is cancelled if there is fraud, misrepresentation or material
-- withholding of information, or the §1.3 condition was not satisfied in a
-- timely fashion, or the one-year policy term (§4.6) has already elapsed.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `policy is cancelled` claim IS
        claim's `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding`
    OR  NOT (`condition 1-3 satisfied by time of hospitalization` claim)
    OR  claim's `months after effective date of hospitalization` GREATER THAN 12

§§ `1.1 - policy in effect`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `policy in effect at time of hospitalization` claim IS
    NOT (`policy is cancelled` claim)

§ `Benefits`

§§ `2.1 - qualifying medical event`

-- Benefits are payable only for hospitalization resulting from sickness or
-- an ACCIDENTAL injury. An injury that the claimant inflicted on themselves
-- deliberately (as opposed to an unintended, unforeseen mishap) is not
-- "accidental", so it does not meet this threshold even though it is not
-- separately listed among the §3.1 exclusions.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `qualifying medical event` claim IS
    CONSIDER claim's `nature of medical event`
    WHEN Sickness            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Accidental Injury` THEN NOT (claim's `injury was self-inflicted and intentional`)

§§ `2.2 - where the benefit is payable`

-- The Daily Hospital Income Benefit is only payable for days of continuous
-- confinement in a hospital in the United States.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `benefit location requirement met` claim IS
    claim's `hospitalized in a hospital in the United States`

§ `General Exclusions`

§§ `3.1 - exclusions`

-- Exclusions 1-4 require that the sickness or injury arise directly or
-- indirectly OUT OF the listed activity: merely being engaged in, or
-- employed for, that activity at the time of hospitalization is not enough
-- on its own unless it actually caused the sickness or injury. Age is a
-- standalone, non-causal exclusion.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an exclusion applies` claim IS
        claim's `arose from skydiving`
    OR  claim's `arose from service in the military`
    OR  claim's `arose from service as a fire fighter`
    OR  claim's `arose from service in the police`
    OR  claim's `age at hospitalization` AT LEAST 80

§ `Coverage Determination`

-- Top-level rule: is a given claim covered under the policy?
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `covered` claim IS
        `policy in effect at time of hospitalization` claim
    AND `qualifying medical event` claim
    AND `benefit location requirement met` claim
    AND NOT (`an exclusion applies` claim)

§ `Benefit and Premium Amounts`

-- §5.1 / §5.2 -- named for completeness; no query asks for a dollar amount.
`the Daily Hospital Benefit amount` MEANS 500

`the premium amount` MEANS 2000
